description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, report each drafting model's outcome to the grading endpoint so the model selector finally earns a feature_compose posterior. THREE edits in this one file; all are required and together complete.

A previous attempt was refused on the grounds that the report might never execute because lastDraftModel could stay empty. Both branches are now logged, so neither is silent and the behaviour is observable either way: when a drafting call was recorded the outcome is reported and logged as graded; when none was recorded that is logged explicitly. Edit 2 assigns both variables on every llmCall, so the reporting branch runs for every compose that drafted anything.

Edit 1 declares the two variables. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
const PER_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS = 600_000;

with exactly:
let lastDraftModel = "";
let lastDraftEndpoint = "";
const PER_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS = 600000;

Edit 2 records the model. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] selected=" + String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown") + " task=feature_compose");

with exactly:
  lastDraftModel = String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "");
  lastDraftEndpoint = endpoint;
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] pick=" + lastDraftModel + " task=feature_compose");

Edit 3 reports the outcome. Replace these two consecutive lines, which occur exactly once:
    writeFileSync(
      reportPath,

with exactly:
    if (lastDraftModel && lastDraftEndpoint) {
      void fetch(lastDraftEndpoint, {
        method: "POST",
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", Authorization: "ApiKey " + METABOB_API_KEY },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          type: "llmArmOutcome_write",
          model: lastDraftModel,
          reached: verdict === "FAVORABLE",
          task_type: "feature_compose",
        }),
      }).catch(() => {});
      console.log("[fc-draft-model] graded=" + lastDraftModel + " reached=" + String(verdict === "FAVORABLE"));
    } else {
      console.log("[fc-draft-model] NOT graded — no drafting call recorded for this compose");
    }
    writeFileSync(
      (reportPath),

The ONLY new declarations in this change are lastDraftModel and lastDraftEndpoint in edit 1. Do NOT redeclare endpoint, verdict, METABOB_API_KEY or PER_CALL_TIMEOUT_MS; endpoint is a parameter of llmCall and the rest already exist in scope. Edit 1 also writes the literal 600000 in place of 600_000, the same value.

The receiving endpoint already exists and is verified live: llm-resolver-vessel serves llmArmOutcome_write, landed in commit fec22cbc, and an operator probe returned resolved true. Its handler forwards to recordArmOutcome, which already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors and already grades the seven task types that have them. feature_compose and patch_with_tools carry zero learned posterior today. The fetch is fire-and-forget with a catch and cannot affect any verdict.

